le, #121), queue (`Queued` with the edited text, a refused message too), unqueue (`NotQueued`); blank text is `EmptyMessage`, a pending message is `MessagePending`, a thread on a path the range does not list is `UnknownThread`; ids from the counters, never reused; the file written before memory changes, so a failed write changes nothing; `file_at` the one path → `RangeFileId` rule), `thread_store/waiting.rs` (the sender's side of the store, `pub(crate)`: `QueuedMessage`, `queued(range)` (queued and refused messages on files the range lists, with their `RangeFileId`, in thread, then message order), `waiting_text` (a message's text to post, read again before each post), `pending_draft_notes` (the drafts pending messages own) and `record_if_waiting` (stores a send's result only while the message still waits with the posted text; whether it did)). Depends on `yamt-range` (`Range::entry`, `Range::entries`) and `yamt-merge-core` among `yamt-*`, may use `yamt-gitio`, never tauri (`scripts/arch-check.sh`). Tests: unit tests in `thread_file.rs`, `thread_store/waiting.rs`; `tests/threads.rs` on real temp folders with a `Range` over a `yamt-conflict-repo` repository.
